  "blockingFindings": [
    {
      "id": "IR-E6OP5-01-COLD-READ-RECOVERY",
      "severity": "BLOCKING",
      "status": "OPEN",
      "title": "Durable CAS/index state cannot rehydrate the admitted authority after process loss",
      "claimRejected": "EP7 resolve_stored_evaluation and Evidence v6 journal recovery provide a complete durable same-store authority path across process restart.",
      "evidence": [
        "EP7 declares that resolve_stored_evaluation(evaluationAuthoritySealRef) reads index/CAS only through the trusted port and reruns exact admission.",
        "Each EP7 EvaluationAuthorityIndexV1 row is closed to schemaVersion, projectId, evaluationAuthoritySealRef and evaluationAuthorityAdmissionRef; it contains no complete-candidate inventory or reconstruction commitment.",
        "The executable store state separately holds _candidates, initializes it empty on store open, populates it only after same-process authorize_evaluation, and makes resolve_stored_evaluation fail when that cache entry is absent.",
        "An independent cold-read probe opened each of the seven already-populated trusted fixtures. Every fixture had one durable index row and five CAS keys but zero cached candidates; all seven resolve calls rejected with 'stored-read has no store-admitted candidate reconstruction'.",
        "After a successful authorization, warm resolve passed. Rebuilding a fresh store from the exact post-authorization CAS/index image again produced zero cached candidates and the same rejection.",
        "Evidence v6 correctly rejects an old handle on a newly opened port because the store-instance token differs. Since cold resolve cannot mint a new handle, there is no accepted authority input for commit_run after restart.",
        "Even a new port over the still-live in-memory state mints a new-token handle; the old FinalizedSemanticEvidenceV1 and PreparedCustodyV1 reject against it. No durable rehydration API is implemented by the Evidence v6 checker.",
        "RunFreePreparedCommitV1 names semanticEvidenceCasRef and preparedCustodyToken but specifies no durable candidate/authority reconstruction root or exact new-port remint/rebind procedure. Its prose recovery rule therefore depends on the missing EP7 reconstruction.",
        "The direct failed-recovery probe left all six final record classes empty, so no partial publication occurred; the defect is liveness/recoverability and claimed mechanism completeness, not an observed atomic leak."
      ],
      "attack": {
        "name": "COLD-PROCESS-LOSS-AFTER-AUTHORITY-ADMISSION",
        "result": "REQUIRED RECOVERY OPERATION IS UNAVAILABLE",
        "steps": [
          "Authorize the exact accepted candidate through a valid host-created project store port.",
          "Persist only the contract-declared immutable CAS rows and EvaluationAuthorityIndexV1 rows.",
          "Lose all process objects, including _candidates, store-instance token, admitted handle, finalized evidence and prepared custody capabilities.",
          "Open a new valid ProjectStoreAuthorityV1 over the same durable project image.",
          "Attempt resolve_stored_evaluation(EASRef), then attempt Evidence v6 recovery/finalization."
        ],
        "observed": [
          "Old handle plus new port rejects store-instance continuity.",
          "Fresh stored resolve rejects because the candidate cache is absent.",
          "No new admitted handle is available to rebind rehydrated Evidence/custody.",
          "The advertised journal/no-index-link retry cannot reach commit_run."
        ],
        "whyExistingChecksMissIt": "EP7 check() and selftest call authorize_evaluation before every successful stored read, preserving _candidates. Evidence v6 tests only live same-process handles and an in-memory ledger keyed by the live store-instance token; neither suite drops process memory and rebuilds from durable rows."
      },
      "impact": [
        "EP7's live caller/store separation is sound, but its durable stored-read contract is not demonstrated by, and is contradicted by, the executable packet.",
        "Evidence v6 crash-after-journal, retry and lost-process recovery claims are incomplete because commit_run requires a live handle/custody set that the durable state cannot reconstruct.",
        "The OP5 G19 candidate mechanism inherits the incomplete Evidence v6 finalization/recovery path and cannot be accepted as a complete design mechanism.",
        "IR-E5OP4-01 and R17-P1A-RR13-01 cannot be marked fully closed by this packet.",
        "No candidate application, product qualification, G19 promotion, CD-RT-5 disposition, integration or seal is authorized."
      ],
      "requiredChange": [
        "Define a closed durable authority-reconstruction record or a deterministic, exact traversal rooted in EvaluationAuthorityIndexV1 that reconstructs every EvaluationAuthorityCandidateV1 field from trusted CAS alone; bind its complete inventory/closure and reject missing, extra, duplicate or conflicting rows.",
        "Keep all store/index capabilities outside candidate JSON. The repair must preserve the opaque host-created ProjectStoreAuthorityV1 boundary and must not serialize store-instance or transaction tokens.",
        "Remove the resolver's dependence on process-local _candidates. Add a cold-start positive that rebuilds the store from durable CAS/index only, resolves the same EAS into a new-port handle, rechecks C2/RI/raw/semantic identities and rejects incomplete or ambiguous reconstruction.",
        "Specify Evidence v6 restart semantics: reopen the project port, remint the admitted handle, and rehydrate FinalizedSemanticEvidenceV1 and PreparedCustodyV1 from durable journal/CAS state under the new port token while preserving exact ProjectId/EAS/admission and content identities.",
        "Execute crash probes before journal, after journal, during the six-write transaction, after commit before response, and from one-sided index/link states in a fresh process. Require no partial publication, exact idempotent convergence and LEDGER.CORRUPT on one-sided/conflicting state.",
        "Regenerate EP, RT, VERSIONING, Evidence, OPERABILITY and response pins and obtain another independent combined rereview."
      ]
    }
  ],
